   "html_text": "Now ‘type’ is a very overworked word. Tokens of that type, to use one of its meanings (roughly as abstract syntactic object), have sometimes been used to stand for properties, including higher-order properties, as in Russell’s various type theories. Church was to continue this tradition in his simple typed version of ⟦M⟧ -calculus (Church, 1940). In this usage, types, such as the property of caninity or of being a shape, have instances such as Fido, in the first case, or the lower-order property",
